{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The third time</b><br>\"Who is this who looks forth.\" The congregation of Israel was praiseworthy until baseless hatred entered among them, and this is the matter that the congregation of Israel said: \"I did not know\" — as one who says, I did not perceive until I caused it for myself, and this is \"my soul set me among the chariots of my noble people,\" for he is the prince of chariots among the nations of the world — the opposite of \"and you shall tread upon their high places.\"" "דגול. Excellent, like הדגל (the standard/banner)." "<b>The third time</b><br>And all that Solomon recounted from the beginning, \"My beloved is white and ruddy,\" until this point — is the deed of the Shekhinah, for thought cannot contain it, nor can the eye behold it; therefore he recounted its actions, and they testify to it." "צח. His deeds are pure/upright." "ואדום. Like consuming fire to the wicked, as in the matter of \"Why is your garment red?\" [Isaiah 63:2]." "דגול. Thousands upon thousands serve Him."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Resolved abbreviations: כנס׳ ישר׳ = congregation of Israel; the final quote appears to cite Isaiah 41:25 or a similar verse; the phrase נדיב מרכבות is textually difficult and rendered hyper-literally.", 2 "Resolved והם יודו עליה as 'they testify to it'; alternatively 'they will acknowledge it.'", 3 "The parenthetical (זכים ל)ישרים shows a variant or correction; rendered as the corrected reading ישרים with זכים implied.", 5 "Rendered the suffix as referring to God, though contextually it may refer to the beloved; ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:52.905765781Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}